70624b2-1550-441e-a8cc-963b68ef9b42-6\\nfc_3c7b8d1c-c619-992f-a7dc-8094a9d63989_2\",\"tool_call\":{\"shellToolCall\":{\"args\":{\"command\":\"gh issue view 15 && echo \\\"===== COMMENTS =====\\\" && gh issue view 15 --comments && echo \\\"===== ISSUE 4 =====\\\" && gh issue view 4\",\"workingDirectory\":\"\",\"timeout\":30000,\"toolCallId\":\"call-c70624b2-1550-441e-a8cc-963b68ef9b42-6\\nfc_3c7b8d1c-c619-992f-a7dc-8094a9d63989_2\",\"simpleCommands\":[\"gh\",\"echo\",\"gh\",\"echo\",\"gh\"],\"hasInputRedirect\":false,\"hasOutputRedirect\":false,\"parsingResult\":{\"parsingFailed\":false,\"executableCommands\":[{\"name\":\"gh\",\"args\":[{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"issue\"},{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"view\"},{\"type\":\"number\",\"value\":\"15\"}],\"fullText\":\"gh issue view 15\"},{\"name\":\"echo\",\"args\":[{\"type\":\"string\",\"value\":\"\\\"===== COMMENTS =====\\\"\"}],\"fullText\":\"echo \\\"===== COMMENTS =====\\\"\"},{\"name\":\"gh\",\"args\":[{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"issue\"},{\"type\":\"word\",\"value\":\"view\"},{\"type\":\"number\",\"value\": [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./tests/fixtures/claude/review-29.stdout","matches":[{"lineNumber":16,"content":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01FKmuBycHsHLwxJT2vZ2UYd\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"title:\\trefactor: backend split behind a Backend enum (#15)\\nstate:\\tDRAFT\\nauthor:\\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\\nlabels:\\t\\nassignees:\\t\\nreviewers:\\t\\nprojects:\\t\\nmilestone:\\t\\nnumber:\\t29\\nurl:\\thttps://github.com/user/delegate/pull/29\\nadditions:\\t1080\\ndeletions:\\t824\\nauto-merge:\\tdisabled\\n--\\nFixes #15\\n\\n- `Backend` enum (cursor only), with one `match` per method: `from_name`, `bin`, `argv`, `spawn`. The job runner's test seam is the `Runner` trait.\\n- `BackendResult` is normalized: text, session id, usage, reported cost, error, duration. Cost comes from the backend when it reports one, otherwise from the model table.\\n- The argv, capability flags, binary resolution and doctor probes moved into `backends/cursor`. `capability.rs` and `cursor_bin.rs` are deleted.\\n- A table-driven parser test runs on every `tests/fixtures/cursor/*.stdout`.\\n- No cursor- [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./tests/fixtures/claude/review-27.stdout","matches":[{"lineNumber":17,"content":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01MGvfzL6aMcxv5m2R4jH5Nh\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"title:\\tSpec: delegate, a multi-backend CLI replacing the cursor-delegate MCP server\\nstate:\\tOPEN\\nauthor:\\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\\nlabels:\\tready-for-agent\\ncomments:\\t1\\nassignees:\\t\\nprojects:\\t\\nmilestone:\\t\\nissue-type:\\t\\nparent:\\t\\nsub-issues:\\t\\nsub-issues-completed:\\t\\nblocked-by:\\t\\nblocking:\\t\\nnumber:\\t4\\n--\\n## Problem Statement\\n\\ncursor-delegate lets a host agent hand work to Cursor's models, but only Cursor's, and only from hosts that load its MCP server. The models I actually use are spread across three harnesses: Cursor (Composer, Grok), pi (ChatGPT-subscription GPT models, opencode-go models) and Claude Code (Claude on the Max plan). None of them can reach the others' models.\\n\\nThe tool has also grown more surface than it uses. Across 413 real `cursor_run` calls, every one ran in the background, `plan` capability was never used, `allow [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":36,"content":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01TaUnFiEBESS12k6BZ22W1U\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"<persisted-output>\\nOutput too large (90.6KB). Full output saved to: /Users/user/.claude/projects/-Users-user-work-delegate-13-contract/955b7c74-9c45-4512-b530-d243dea4139a/tool-results/b0l0bw9d3.txt\\n\\nPreview (first 2KB):\\n    }\\n    Ok(out)\\n}\\n\\nfn decode_host_profile(raw: Option<&Value>) -> Result<HostProfile, String> {\\n    let Some(raw) = raw else {\\n        return Ok(HostProfile::default());\\n    };\\n    if raw.is_null() {\\n        return Ok(HostProfile::default());\\n    }\\n    let obj = raw\\n        .as_object()\\n        .ok_or_else(|| \\\"invalid config: host profile must be an object\\\".to_string())?;\\n    let mut profile = HostProfile::default();\\n    if let Some(d) = opt_str(obj, \\\"default\\\", \\\"host-profile\\\")? {\\n        profile.default = Some(d);\\n    }\\n    if let Some(models) = obj.get(\\\"models\\\") {\\n        profile.models = Some(decode_models [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./tests/fixtures/claude/review-26.stdout","matches":[{"lineNumber":15,"content":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01L6KyEPLtkYfZ51x8BQR2oQ\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"<persisted-output>\\nOutput too large (30.1KB). Full output saved to: /Users/user/.claude/projects/-Users-user-work-delegate-12-budgets/bc26522a-3803-4d63-8d60-9a2a2108782c/tool-results/b3qm7xeoz.txt\\n\\nPreview (first 2KB):\\ntitle:\\ttest: latency and supervisor-memory budgets (#12)\\nstate:\\tDRAFT\\nauthor:\\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\\nlabels:\\t\\nassignees:\\t\\nreviewers:\\t\\nprojects:\\t\\nmilestone:\\t\\nnumber:\\t26\\nurl:\\thttps://github.com/user/delegate/pull/26\\nadditions:\\t338\\ndeletions:\\t0\\nauto-merge:\\tdisabled\\n--\\nFixes #12\\n\\n`tests/budgets.rs` adds a wall-clock budget for each command, measured against fake agents: run, resume, cancel, watch on a terminal job, doctor, and models. It also adds a resident-memory budget for the supervisor while a fake agent runs. Each budget is about 3x the local median, with the measured value in a comment. No production code [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,