ed by SHA, the token is read-only, and `pull_request_target` is not used.\\n\\nImplemented by composer-2.5 via `scripts/record.sh` (fixture lands with #18).\\n\\nCo-authored with Claude Code.\\ndiff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml\\nnew file mode 100644\\nindex 0000000..ede11d5\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml\\n@@ -0,0 +1,23 @ [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./tests/fixtures/claude/review-18.stdout","matches":[{"lineNumber":15,"content":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01HGCobLa7Nx9QjMUKTdjMFz\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"title:\\ttest: recording script and redacted headless fixtures (#6)\\nstate:\\tDRAFT\\nauthor:\\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\\nlabels:\\t\\nassignees:\\t\\nreviewers:\\t\\nprojects:\\t\\nmilestone:\\t\\nnumber:\\t18\\nurl:\\thttps://github.com/user/delegate/pull/18\\nadditions:\\t1972\\ndeletions:\\t0\\nauto-merge:\\tdisabled\\n--\\nFixes #6\\n\\n- `scripts/record.sh BACKEND MODEL CAPABILITY NAME [CWD] [SESSION] < prompt` runs one prompt through cursor-agent, pi or claude with the flags spec #4 assigns. It writes `tests/fixtures/<backend>/NAME.{stdout,stderr,argv}`. `CANCEL_AFTER=N` records a run cancelled with SIGTERM.\\n- `scripts/redact.jq` strips the recording user's setup (pi system-prompt sections and extension tool schemas; Claude init lists and hook output). The home-directory name is replaced with `user`.\\n- 22 recorded runs across cursor, pi and Claude: plain answer, tool calls, r [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":20,"content":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01FKZWbvxr8HjdhvcCbZixe8\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"     1\\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n     2\\t# Run one prompt through a backend's raw headless CLI and save stdout/stderr as a parser fixture.\\n     3\\t#\\n     4\\t#   scripts/record.sh BACKEND MODEL CAPABILITY NAME [CWD] [SESSION] < prompt\\n     5\\t#\\n     6\\t# BACKEND: cursor | pi | claude. CAPABILITY: read-only | read-write (pi rejects read-only).\\n     7\\t# SESSION resumes that backend session; pi and claude get a fresh id when it is omitted.\\n     8\\t# CANCEL_AFTER=N sends the CLI SIGTERM after N seconds.\\n     9\\t# Writes tests/fixtures/BACKEND/NAME.{stdout,stderr,argv}; prints the session id (if chosen) and exit code.\\n    10\\tset -uo pipefail\\n    11\\t\\n    12\\t[ $# -ge 4 ] || { sed -n 2,9p \\\"$0\\\"; exit 2; }\\n    13\\tbackend=$1 model=$2 cap=$3 name=$4 cwd=${5:-$PWD} session=${6:-}\\n    14\\there=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\n    15\\tout=\\\"$here/../t [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./scripts/record.sh","matches":[{"lineNumber":30,"content":"    [ \"$cap\" = read-only ] && { echo \"pi cannot enforce read-only\" >&2; exit 2; }","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":48,"totalMatchedLines":48,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_00fde086-493c-46f5-8dd6-6ea6dda1a38","startedAtMs":"1790856486400","completedAtMs":"1790856486832"},"model_call_id":"8c794d25-ac97-4ac1-895c-17b2e5b73d11-3-ier4","session_id":"59d11db8-30ee-4975-b72e-e79848d2a033","timestamp_ms":1790856486759}
